## 5. ⚠️ Critical Anti-Patterns (AZDJ Protocol — Never Revert)

### AP-1: Emulator Project Lock
```bash
# ALWAYS verify the emulator is running for the correct project
grep -i "<correct-project>\\|wrong-project" /tmp/infinity-emulator.log
# Wrong project → pkill -f "firebase emulators" && restart
```

### AP-2: Firestore via REST, Not UI
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT — deterministic, no timeout, no UI flake
await page.request.post(`${FIRESTORE}/leads?documentId=${leadId}`, { data: {...} });
await page.request.patch(`${FIRESTORE}/leads/${leadId}?updateMask.fieldPaths=status`, {...});

// ❌ WRONG — UI flows have timeouts, async leadId race conditions
await page.goto('/questionnaire'); // fragile
```

### AP-3: Never Use networkidle on Firebase Pages
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT — Firebase WebSocket keeps network perpetually busy
await page.waitForLoadState('domcontentloaded');
await page.locator('#target').waitFor({ state: 'visible', timeout: 15000 });

// ❌ WRONG — will ALWAYS timeout on any page with Firestore real-time listener
await page.waitForLoadState('networkidle');
```

### AP-4: Never Hardcode a Port in Tests
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT — uses Playwright baseURL from config
await page.goto('/checkout');

// ❌ WRONG — port mismatch will silently fail in CI or on port change
await page.goto('http://localhost:5005/checkout');
```

### AP-5: Parallel Link Validation
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT — request is concurrent-safe
const response = await page.context().request.get(link);

// ❌ WRONG — page.goto in Promise.all causes race conditions
await Promise.all(links.map(l => page.goto(l)));
```

### AP-6: E2E Email Capture Pattern
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT — Cloud Function writes to e2e_mock_emails collection in emulator
// NEVER check a real mailbox in tests; NEVER mock sendEmail at the test level
const emails = await page.request.get(
  'http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1/projects/<PROJECT_ID>/databases/(default)/documents/e2e_mock_emails'
);
const subjects = (await emails.json()).documents.map(d => d.fields.subject.stringValue);
expect(subjects).toContain('Order Confirmed');
```

